==Dutch==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|aːr|lang=nl}}
* {{a|Netherlands}} {{IPA|/ʋaːr/|lang=nl}}
* {{a|Belgium, Suriname}} {{IPA|/waːr/|lang=nl}}
* {{audio|Nl-waar.ogg|audio|lang=nl}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|nl|dum|waer}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|*war}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*hwar}}. Cognate with English {{m|en|where}}.

====Adverb====
{{nl-adv}}

# {{label|nl|interrogative}} [[where]], in which place
#: '''''Waar''' is Jan?''
#:: '''Where''' is John?
# {{label|nl|relative}} [[where]], the place that
#: ''Dit is '''waar''' hij woont.''
#:: This is '''where''' he lives.
# {{label|nl|interrogative|with a preposition}} [[what]], which thing
#: '''''Waar''' is dat goed voor?''
#:: '''What''' is that good for?
# {{label|nl|relative|with a preposition}} [[what]], that which
#: ''Dit is '''waar''' dat goed voor is''
#:: This is '''what''' that is good for.

====Usage notes====
With a preposition, {{m|nl||waar}} is used instead of {{m|nl|wat}} to create a [[pronominal adverb]]. See also [[:Category:Dutch pronominal adverbs]].

====Derived terms====
See [[:Category:Dutch pronominal adverbs]]

